# Option menus

For three-dot / overflow / actions menus (e.g. event card, library board):

## Rows
- Each option: icon + label with `flex items-center gap-2`, **left-aligned**.
- Do **not** use `justify-between` just for icon + label - that pushes text to the right.
- Trailing status only when real (e.g. “Copied!”): keep label left (`flex-1` / `min-w-0`), status `shrink-0` on the right.
- Icons: same size and muted color treatment on every row (`size={14}`, `text-gray-500` / neutral equivalent).

## Typography
- One label style for all options: `text-sm` (no mixed weights or sizes for peer items).

## Dividers
- Dividers only **between groups** (e.g. share actions vs edit/delete), never on random individual rows.
- Prefer a single `border-t` separator element (or one bordered group start), not scattered `border-t` on some buttons.

## Placement
- Anchor the panel to the trigger; don’t invent one-off left/right alignment schemes per menu.

## Example

```tsx
// ❌ BAD - label shoved right
<button className="… flex items-center justify-between">
  <Share2 size={14} />
  <span>Copy link</span>
</button>

// ✅ GOOD
<button className="… flex items-center gap-2">
  <Share2 size={14} className="shrink-0 text-gray-500" />
  <span>Copy link</span>
</button>
```
